Ping Pong (Pong) is a classic two‑dimensional table tennis game where two paddles
hit a ball back and forth across a playfield. The objective is simple: deflect the ball 
past your opponent’s paddle to score. This web version uses an HTML5 canvas for rendering
and straightforward physics for smooth, responsive play on both desktop and mobile devices.

Why I created this I built this PingPong game as a small, focused project to learn and demonstrate
practical game programming techniques: frame‑rate‑independent movement, touch and keyboard controls, 
simple AI difficulty, and persistent settings via localStorage. It’s also a playground for experimenting 
with gameplay feel—such as adding spin and refining collision responses—so I can iterate quickly and share
improvements. Finally, I wanted to make an easy-to-run, accessible demo that others can fork, tinker with, and 
use as a starting point for their own game experiments.

